# motoquencer: the "randomize CV" lane (fadermode 1) at its bottom detent.
# motoquencer.md: "Randomize CV is a number from 0 (fader at the bottom) to 7
# (fader at the top). 0 means randomization is off." This pins BOTH halves of
# "off": the step's CV never moves, and — just as importantly — a step entry with
# randomization off must not draw from the engine RNG at all.
#
# The RNG pin works by spending the seed-1 xorshift stream visibly: after two full
# turns of four un-randomized steps, a luckycvs trigger draws four chance coins
# (luckychance 1 -> every step targeted) and then four fresh CVs, i.e. draws 5..8
# of the stream. Continuous pitch (cvbase 0, cvrange 1) makes CV == cvpos, so the
# rerolled steps 3 and 4 must be exactly those seed-1 values. If a step entry ever
# consumed a draw of its own, these two numbers would move.
seed 1
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    numfaders = 4
    quantize  = 0
    cvbase    = 0
    cvrange   = 1
    holdcv    = 0
    clock     = I1
    fadermode = I3
    luckycvs  = I2
    cv        = O1
>>>
# step 1's randomize fader goes to the top detent (7) and back down to 0 again
@1 set I3 1
@2 move F1 1.0
@3 expect F1 1.0 tol 1e-4
@4 move F1 0.0
@5 set I3 0
# dial four distinct pitches on the CV lane
@6 move F1 0.1
@6 move F2 0.2
@6 move F3 0.3
@6 move F4 0.4
# two turns: the same four CVs, to the last digit
@10 set I1 1
@10 expect O1 0.1 tol 1e-5
@11 set I1 0
@12 set I1 1
@12 expect O1 0.2 tol 1e-5
@13 set I1 0
@14 set I1 1
@14 expect O1 0.3 tol 1e-5
@15 set I1 0
@16 set I1 1
@16 expect O1 0.4 tol 1e-5
@17 set I1 0
@18 set I1 1
@18 expect O1 0.1 tol 1e-5
@19 set I1 0
@20 set I1 1
@20 expect O1 0.2 tol 1e-5
@21 set I1 0
# luckycvs: 4 coins + 4 CVs off an untouched seed-1 stream
@22 set I2 1
@23 set I2 0
@24 set I1 1
@24 expect O1 0.147250 tol 1e-5
@25 set I1 0
@26 set I1 1
@26 expect O1 0.101457 tol 1e-5
